language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Give every person one slot from their own wish list, within the slot capacities, so that as many people as possible get their first wish.
given n_people, n_slots, max_wishes : int(1..)
given capacity : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_slots)] of int(0..)
$ wishes[p, k] is the k-th wish of person p; padded with 0 after wishes_len[p]
given wishes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_people), int(1..max_wishes)] of int(0..n_slots)
given wishes_len : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_people)] of int(1..max_wishes)
$ choice[p] is the position in p's wish list that p gets
find choice : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_people)] of int(1..max_wishes)
find slot : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_people)] of int(1..n_slots)
find first_wishes : int(0..n_people)
maximising first_wishes
such that
$ a person only gets a slot from their own list
forAll p : int(1..n_people) . choice[p] <= wishes_len[p],
forAll p : int(1..n_people) . slot[p] = wishes[p, choice[p]],
$ no slot holds more people than its capacity
atmost(slot, capacity, [s | s : int(1..n_slots)]),
$ count the people who get their first wish
first_wishes = (sum p : int(1..n_people) . toInt(choice[p] = 1))
